  "description": "YUKTEF crystallizes in the cubic crystal system with space group I -4 3 d. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H75 Cu6 Dy3 F18 N6 O24,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cu3 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu4 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cu5 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu6 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.136-3.816 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.65-113.45°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy3Cu6(L1)6(μ3-OH)6(H2O)6(OH)6]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(I), I(II).",
